id: sake-bottle
name: Sake Bottle
kind: gear
tags: food
craftDC: Qualified
# Its Details.
details: food
# "When this item is created, it holds 4 stacks of Alcohol and cannot hold more than 4."
chargesDice: 4
chargesLabel: Alcohol
# "You can spend 1 Action and 1 Alcohol from the Sake Bottle to enter the Drunk Special State until
# the start of your next turn." The card says it; Drunk is a Special State now (states/drunk.dbu), its Level set on the sheet.
placeCost: 1
chargeUseLabel: Drink
chargeUseNote: enters the Drunk Special State until the start of their next turn
# "When it has no Alcohol left in it, it can be used for the Sealing Unique Ability."
sealContainer: true
sealWhenEmpty: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Holds 4 Alcohol. An Action and 1 Alcohol: Drunk until the start of your next turn.
text: >
  Sake Bottle [Food]: A flask, gourd, or other drink container which you can fill with your choice
  of drink.
  –Craft DC: Qualified
  –Details: Food
  –Effects: When this item is created, it holds 4 stacks of Alcohol and cannot hold more than 4
  stacks of Alcohol. You can spend 1 Action and 1 Alcohol from the Sake Bottle to enter the Drunk
  Special State until the start of your next turn.

  You can refill your Sake Bottle while Adventuring, but when it has no Alcohol left in it, it can
  be used for the Sealing Unique Ability.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 4 Alcohol when given, shown on its row and editable on the Item. Drink, on its row: 1 Action and 1
# Alcohol, and the card says they are Drunk until the start of their next turn.
#
# --- What is not built -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Drunk Special State (the card says it; the table applies it). Refilling while Adventuring -
# set its Alcohol back on the Item, up to 4. The Sealing Unique Ability it can hold when empty.
